prop fp_ledge else.open=message||A card lock on the box - a Tangaroa keycard would open it.

# --- Settings, story items, notes, behaviours, quest ------------------------------------------------------------------
info title=The Foundation Piles
info author=Custom Islands
info description=Under Highwater: a forest of giant stone piles ten metres down, two of them cracked, shoring jacks at their feet, air round their foot-blocks - and a stingray grown huge among them. A dry mudflat at the city's edge. The last of The City That Never Sank.
island on.arrive=message||A grey mudflat at the city's edge. Beyond it the water goes black - and down there, the piles the whole city stands on.

story jack1|Pile 1 jacked|Bolt|The first pile, shored up.
story jack2|Pile 2 jacked|Bolt|The second pile, shored up.
story jack3|Pile 3 jacked|Bolt|The third pile, shored up.
story jack4|Pile 4 jacked|Bolt|The fourth pile, shored up - the city holds.
story rayhurt|Pile stingray wounded|Bolt|You wounded the stingray that nests among the piles.
story raydown|Pile stingray defeated|Bolt|The pile stingray is dead. The piles are yours to mend.

prop piles tint.color=#6e6a60
prop piles tint.amount=0.5
prop skyline tint.color=#5a6068
prop skyline tint.amount=0.5
prop stormsound sound.event=event:/amb/rain_ocean
prop stormsound sound.volume=0.6
prop stormsound zone.radius=70
prop puffers creature.count=2
prop pileray creature.count=1
prop pileray creature.respawn=0
prop pileray creature.size=3
prop pileray creature.health=10
prop pileray boss.phase=0.5
prop pileray boss.summon=2
prop pileray tint.color=#3c4a40
prop pileray tint.amount=0.6
prop pileray on.phase=give||story:rayhurt*1\nmessage||The stingray thrashes against a pile - and two more come out of the dark to help it.
prop pileray on.defeat=signal||raydown\ngive||story:rayhurt*1\ngive||story:raydown*1\nmessage||The great stingray drifts down between the piles and lies still. The last two jacks are clear.
prop closing beh.hidden=1
prop closing obj.name=closing

prop jack1 beh.use=Wind the first pile's jack
prop jack1 if.use=!signal|jack1
prop jack1 on.use=signal||jack1\ngive||story:jack1*1\nsound||event:/raft/radar/lever\nmessage||The jack bites. Above you the pile groans - and stops leaning.
prop jack1 else.use=message||This pile is shored.
prop jack2 beh.use=Wind the second pile's jack
prop jack2 if.use=signal|jack1
prop jack2 on.use=signal||jack2\ngive||story:jack2*1\nsound||event:/raft/radar/lever\nmessage||The second jack bites. In the dark between the piles, something big turns toward the sound.
prop jack2 else.use=message||Rusted solid. The engineer's note says: the first pile first.
prop jack3 beh.use=Wind the third pile's jack
prop jack3 if.use=signal|raydown
prop jack3 on.use=signal||jack3\ngive||story:jack3*1\nsound||event:/raft/radar/lever\nmessage||The third pile takes the weight again.
prop jack3 else.use=message||You can't work the jack with that stingray circling.
prop jack4 beh.use=Wind the fourth pile's jack
prop jack4 if.use=signal|jack3
prop jack4 on.use=signal||jack4\ngive||story:jack4*1\nshow|closing\nsound||event:/raft/radar/lever\nmessage||The last jack bites. All through the water the piles settle. Highwater holds - for now. Tucked behind the jack, a note.
prop jack4 else.use=message||The third pile first.

note enginenote Nell Abernethy's note | Pinned over the old engineer's board, in a clerk's tidy hand -\n\nYou came. Good. I came down on the last barge after the council broke up, and I am writing this on my knee, so forgive the hand.\n\nCouncillor Crane went down the pile stair an hour before me, alone, with a lantern. He has not come back up. The air under the city lies in pockets round the foot-blocks; he knew that - he signed for them every year.\n\nFour piles carry the Crown. The jacks are at their feet. The first pile first, then the second - and then the stingray will wake. The pile drivers left blasting barrels on the piles for it. The third and the fourth after.\n\nBefore you dive, read the engineers' survey in their ruined hut inland, and look at what the rubble bank is made of. Then you will know why the Rookery was weight.\n\nInes's chalk hooks go down the pile stair. Follow them.\n\n- N. Abernethy
note engineerbox Engineer's box | The pile engineer's spare tools.
note closing The city holds | Behind the fourth jack, in a tin with chalk fingerprints on the lid -\n\nYou did it. I heard the piles settle from the stair, all four, like a house letting out its breath.\n\nI found him before you did. I closed his eyes and left his page where it was, for you - you earned the reading of it. Nell will take it up to the Crown. Let the factions argue over it for a hundred years; they are good at that.\n\nI'm going up. Dobbs is waiting on the mudflat with a thermos and a complaint about the tide.\n\nIf you spoke for the Rookery on the roofs, Maud's boats are already out on the shoal ahead, band 700 - Pip has a tram line to build and says you are its first passenger.\n\nThe brass plates on the piles say CONCORD WORKS. Whoever built them is still out there, on the old band. That's another story.\n\n- Ines
note returnsign Mudflat | High-water mark. The tide comes no further.
loot engineerbox Rope*2;MetalIngot*2;Bolt*2
prop engineerbox loot.refill=0

prop mudzone zone.id=mudflat
prop mudzone zone.radius=4
prop mudzone zone.message=The mudflat. The engineer's hut, a board, and the black water beyond.
prop returnzone zone.id=mudflat_return
prop returnzone zone.radius=3
prop returnzone zone.message=Back on the mudflat. Dobbs is there with a thermos, complaining about the tide. Up above, the rain is easing off.

prop blast1 on.use=message||The barrel goes up under the pile - the shock rolls the stingray over.\nhit|pileray|40\nhide|\nsignal||blast
prop blast2 on.use=message||The second barrel bursts - the stingray's hide splits along the old scar.\nhit|pileray|40\nhide|\nsignal||blast
prop blast3 on.use=message||The last barrel blows - and the pile shudders free of the stingray.\nhit|pileray|40\nhide|\nsignal||blast
note diggercrate Excavator's toolbox | The excavator slid off the bank in a storm. Its toolbox stayed bolted to the cab - and in the lid, the driver's work sheets.\n\nNIGHT SHIFT. DIG BALLAST PIT AT THE PILE FOOT. BARGE IRON FROM PUMPCROWN. NO LIGHTS. NO NAMES. Paid in Authority tokens, double.\n\nOn the last sheet, pressed hard: The ground under pile four is moving. I told the Councillor. He said: then dig faster. I have gone up to the Rookery to dig for them instead. Whoever finds this - the drivers kept charges in the cave in the cliff. You will want them down there. - Carver
loot diggercrate MetalIngot*3;Bolt*3;Scrap*3
note engineersurvey Engineers' survey | PILE SURVEY - CROWN FOUNDATIONS\n\nFour piles carry the Crown. Inspected this year: all four sound. Jacks serviced, as funded. Signed every year for twenty-two years, in the same neat hand: A.C.\n\n(Underneath, in pencil, shaky: I was the pile engineer. The service money was voted every year and never spent. He was a junior clerk then, and it paid for his first election. When the cracks came he could not send men down to the jacks - they would have seen the rust, and the dates. So he sent iron instead. I am old and I was paid to keep quiet, and I am sorry. - R. Tolley)\n\n(And in grease pencil: He couldn't wind the jacks without a vote, so he bought weight. Lowstreet's water. The barges' iron. The Rookery's roofs next. - I.M.)
note driverchest Pile-driver's stash | Blasting charges wrapped in oilcloth, and the drivers' pay, never collected.\n\nOn the cave wall above, a chalk hook you know by now, and under it: THE BARRELS ON THE PILES ARE THE SAME CHARGE. THE RAY'S HIDE ONLY GIVES TO A BLAST. LIGHT ONE UNDER IT, NOT UNDER YOU. - I.M.
note jacklog1 Jack log - pile 1 | A brass tag wired to the first jack, stamped once a year -\n\nSERVICED. SOUND. - A.C.\n\nTwenty-two stamps, the same initials, the same neat hand. The grease in the jack's screw is older than the stamps: black, hard as tar, untouched since Concord Works fitted it.\n\nUnder the last stamp, in Ines's grease pencil: Nobody has turned this since before he was born. It still bites, if you lean on it. Wind it - then the second. The stingray sleeps between them, and the second jack will wake it.
note jacklog3 Jack log - pile 3 | The tag on the third jack. Every stamp on it has been scored through with a knife point, and below them, fresh, the newest entry - tonight's:\n\nCRACKED. CRACKED. CRACKED. I SIGNED THEM ALL. - A.C.\n\nLantern soot on the handle. He tried to wind this one before you, and the stingray drove him off it. A long scrape runs along the pile where he went on - past the fourth air pocket, into the dark.
note cranepage Aldous Crane's last page | A notebook page, in the neat hand, getting less neat -\n\nTo whoever winds the fourth.\n\nI was twenty-six, the piles were sound, and the service money paid for my first election. Nobody died of it. For twenty-two years nobody died of it.\n\nThen the cracks. To wind the jacks I would have had to say they had never been seen to. So I gave the Crown weight instead. Water is weight: I opened the valves and let Lowstreet fill. Iron is weight: I sank it here by night. I signed for the factions so that each would think the others knew. Two thousand people, I told myself, were a fair price for a city.\n\nIt was never weight the piles needed. It was someone to come down here and turn a handle. That was all, for twenty-two years.\n\nThe air is going. Number four will not turn while the other three hang loose. Do not let it beat you too.\n\n- A. Crane
loot driverchest ExplosiveGoo*2;TradeToken*3;Rope*2
prop driverchest loot.refill=0
quest title=The Piles
quest intro=The storm is cracking the four piles under the Crown, and Councillor Crane has gone down the pile stair alone. Land on the mudflat at the city's edge - Nell Abernethy left a note there.
step reach|mudflat|1|Land on the flat mud at the city's edge, by the engineer's board
step read|Nell Abernethy's note|1|Read Nell Abernethy's note on the engineer's board
step read|Engineers' survey|1|Read the engineers' survey in their ruined hut inland
step open|Excavator's toolbox|1|Open the toolbox crate of the sunk excavator on the shore
step reach|driver_cave|1|Find the pile drivers' cave in the cliff
step open|Pile-driver's stash|1|Open the pile drivers' stash in the cave
step reach|rubble_bank|1|Climb the rubble bank, the long pile of stone and iron, and see what it is made of
step reach|pile_1|1|Follow Ines's hooks down the pile stair to the first pile
step read|Jack log - pile 1|1|Read the jack log wired to the first jack
step collect|story:jack1|1|Wind the first pile's jack
step reach|pile_2|1|Swim to the second pile
step collect|story:jack2|1|Wind the second pile's jack
step collect|story:rayhurt|1|Blast the stingray that wakes among the piles
step collect|story:raydown|1|Finish the pile stingray
step collect|story:jack3|1|Wind the third pile's jack
step read|Jack log - pile 3|1|Read the jack log on the third jack
step read|Aldous Crane's last page|1|Follow the scrape on the pile to the fourth air pocket and read what is there
step collect|story:jack4|1|Wind the fourth pile's jack
step read|The city holds|1|Read the note behind the last jack
step reach|mudflat_return|1|Go back up to the mudflat
quest done=Highwater holds. Four jacks wound, one confession read, and a city that will have to hear what it stands on. Whatever you chose on the Crown, it will have to live with it.
quest reward=TitaniumOre*2;TradeToken*10

# --- 10-25: the open sand filled - hills where nothing stands, a ruin on the biggest, a wreck, plants over all
# (plan.py from the built island: every hill at least 8 m clear of anything the recipe placed; frame = the land centre)
origin
